# SH863 — line endings are declared here, not left to whoever cloned the repository.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is a *per-machine* setting, so a repository that declares nothing gets a different
# answer per contributor. On the machine this was measured on it is `input`: git stores LF and
# converts nothing on checkout, so a file a Windows editor created keeps CRLF on disk for ever while
# the index holds LF. **308 of 1864 tracked files** were in that state, `cli/src/convert.mjs` and
# `cli/src/diff.mjs` — two of the largest modules in the CLI — among them.
#
# The cost is the review. A one-character change to `convert.mjs` reported:
#
#     git diff --stat                      cli/src/convert.mjs | 4172 ++++----
#     git diff --stat --ignore-cr-at-eol   cli/src/convert.mjs |    2 +-
#
# Four thousand changed lines with the real one somewhere inside them, and `git blame` crediting
# every line to whoever last saved the file. The warning git printed on each such commit — *CRLF will
# be replaced by LF the next time Git touches it* — had been printing long enough to be furniture.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary and leave it alone; `eol=lf` is what makes the working tree the
# same on every machine rather than depending on the clone's own config.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The two kinds that are not LF, and one of them would break.
#
# A Windows batch file is read by `cmd.exe`, which is entitled to care about the carriage return —
# a `goto` label or a line continuation can behave differently without it. `run-commit.cmd` and
# `install-roadkeep.cmd` are how this project commits and installs its own tooling, so this is not
# the place to find out. Shell scripts are the opposite and take LF from the rule above.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Named rather than left to detection. `text=auto` would almost certainly classify these correctly —
# it looks for a NUL in the first 8000 bytes — but "almost certainly" over a font or an image is a
# corrupted file nobody notices until it is served, and the cost of the line is nothing.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary

